.TH SELINUXWHY 1
.SH NAME
selinuxwhy \- summarize recent SELinux AVC denial evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B selinuxwhy
[--audit-log PATH] [--max-denials COUNT] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads SELinux enforcement state and a bounded set of AVC records from an audit
log. It does not alter policy, relabel files, or invoke remediation tools.
Unreadable audit logs are reported as partial visibility.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --audit-log PATH
Audit log to inspect; defaults to /var/log/audit/audit.log.
.TP
.B --max-denials COUNT
Return one through 1000 denial records; the default is 50.
.TP
.B --format json
Emit the versioned JSON report (the only supported format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 means AVC denials were found; 2 invalid usage; 3 partial visibility or no
denials; and 4 a runtime failure.
